    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0494" n="484" sameAs="frus:frus1947v07/pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.0023/1–2147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Dairen</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Benninghoff</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dairen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-01-21">January 21 [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">18</hi>], 1947</date>.<lb/>[Received January
                        21—9:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>12. Clear text in numerals of translation of memorandum from Soviet Consul
                    following telegram.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d386-f1"/> Reference my telegram 10,
                    Jan. 16 [<hi rendition="#italic">17</hi>]. Words in paragraph 3 of “commercial
                    ship” mean unarmed naval vessel is only personal opinion Soviet Consul.</p>
                <pb facs="0495" n="485" xml:id="pg485"/>
                <p>He suggests this point be cleared in Moscow, and apparently wording came from
                    Moscow.</p>
                <p>Will take no action pending instructions.</p>
                <p>Repeat Shanghai, Nanking, Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Benninghoff</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d386-f1" n="11" xml:id="d386-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 13, January 18, <hi rendition="#italic">infra.</hi>
                </p>
